  "slug": "membrane-cholesterol-0cb8",
  "summary": "Simulation and scattering now quantify how protein inclusions and condensates perturb bilayer thickness, lipid interdigitation, and membrane elasticity.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is how proteins and condensates mechanically perturb lipid bilayers. A preprint combining all-atom MD, multiscale SAXS and Bayesian inference quantifies OmpLA-induced membrane strain and protein/lipid ratio in proteoliposomes. A coarse-grained MD study reports that enhanced lipid interdigitation beneath protein condensates mediates transbilayer coupling. A reaction-diffusion model distinguishes three client-exchange regimes governing FRAP recovery in scaffold-driven condensates. Methodologically, a published SuAVE implementation computes membrane area compressibility by direct surface-area integration, avoiding Fourier wavevector cutoffs. A proteome-scale study quantifies interactions driving IDP condensate formation, extending the thread toward condensate assembly. The new elements are interdigitation as a transbilayer coupling mechanism and combined MD-SAXS-Bayesian strain quantification. The exchange and proteome papers address condensate kinetics and formation rather than membrane mechanics directly.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-12"
}
